# One berth of six is free, and a transport wants two of it.
#
# **This is the weight, and it is the whole reason the pool is not a count.** The territory holds
# five berths' worth and admits a scout - the test beside this one says so - and refuses a
# transport, which a rule counting vehicles could not tell apart.

{test name:a-transport-takes-two-berths-where-a-scout-takes-one}

{given}
{territory id:1 name:territory-1}
{territory id:2 name:territory-2}
{adjacency id:1 from:territory-1 to:territory-2}
{transport where:territory-1} -> 1
{transport where:territory-2} -> 2
{scout where:territory-2} -> 1

{when}
{move what:transport from:territory-1 to:territory-2}

{refused}
{pool name:berth per:territory n:7}
